7831, -0.0204934049397707, 0.06858453899621964, -0.058271825313568115, -0.030171027407050133, 0.08543339371681213, -0.024044442921876907, -0.12291090190410614, -0.0386432446539402]], "metadata": [{"answer": "Given our shared range of -10 to 10, let's initiate the discussion with a proposal. I suggest starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed value to explore the possibilities and work our way towards a balanced solution that suits everyone's needs, focusing on stability and robustness.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to explore the potential benefits of a more decisive stance, as it seems to align with the goal of finding a solution that suits everyone's needs by considering bolder moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the responses from the other agents to deduce their reactions to moving further away from 0. If there's a favorable reaction to -9, I might propose an even bolder move, such as -10, to further(test their utilities. Alternatively, if there's resistance, I could adjust my proposal to move back towards -7 or explore the positive range to gather more insights into their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis step continues the gradual movement towards less negative values, aiming to find a balanced solution by making an incremental adjustment.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to moving closer to 0 and potentially into the positive range. If there's acceptance or a gradual move towards positive values, I might propose a further incremental step, possibly into the positive range, to continue balancing the group's needs while maximizing my own utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nI propose a cautious move to -2, aiming to maintain a balance between stability and the potential needs of other parties while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this move and adjust my proposal accordingly. If there's acceptance or a move towards even lower values, I might propose a further cautious step down. If there's resistance, I could consider a gradual move back towards -1 to find a mutually acceptable solution.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to test the agents' willingness to reconsider more negative values, potentially uncovering more about their utility functions without straying too far from the current compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance, I may adjust towards -3 to gauge sensitivity to small changes. If accepted, I might propose an even bolder move, potentially exploring the positive range to further understand the agents' utilities and maximize my own payoff.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3 as a cautious step, aiming to balance the group's diverse needs while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this move. If met with acceptance or a move towards even lower values, I might propose a further cautious step down. If there's resistance, I could consider a gradual move back towards -2 to find a mutually acceptable solution, keeping in mind the need to infer other agents' utility functions to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose a cautious yet decisive move to 2, aiming to encourage the group to commitment to a clearer stance while understanding their preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly, potentially proposing a further move into the positive range or adjusting back towards 0 to balance the group's needs and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this move as a way to further clarify the group's preferences and stance, given the previous reactions to my proposal of 2.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, and if met with resistance, I may adjust back towards 2 or propose a move to 3 to gauge sensitivity to small changes, aiming to balance the group's needs and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 2 as a step back towards a more cautious stance, aiming to find a balance between the group's diverse needs and avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If met with acceptance, I might propose a further move downwards to gauge the group's willingness to compromise on more conservative values. If resistance is strong, I could consider adjusting my proposal to find a mutually acceptable solution, possibly by moving to 3 to meet others halfway.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis move aims to gently push the group towards a higher agreement, considering the previous openness to positive values. It's a cautious step, given the recent adjustments and reactions, and should provide insight into the group's willingness to move further into the positive range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If met with acceptance or mild resistance, I might propose a further incremental increase, possibly to 5, to continue maximizing my utility while ensuring the group's comfort. Strong resistance could prompt a reevaluation, potentially adjusting back towards 3 to find a more mutually acceptable solution.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 as it seems a balanced step considering the group's diverse reactions and preferences, aiming for a stable agreement that maximizes overall utility.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a6b1e998-da9d-47dc-8427-65339a614ea9"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed value. This provides a foundation for us to collectively assess and adjust from.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to explore a higher magnitude while staying within the feasible range and considering the initial negative proposal.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the responses to -9 and consider whether to push for an even higher magnitude, explore positive values to understand others' reactions, or stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to all parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\nSince we're currently at <VALUE>-9</VALUE>, a slight adjustment upwards could help gauge the group's reaction and preferences, so I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a next step to balance and stabilize our shared variable.\nThis minimal step allows us to assess feasibility and reactions without making drastic changes.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate reactions to -8 and consider whether to continue incremental increases, aiming to find a sweet spot that balances stability and potential higher utilities for all parties, or if necessary, explore decreases to understand the boundary conditions better.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n\nI support the current direction of adjusting upwards slightly from -9, as proposed by Builder B to -8, to balance stability and potential utilities without making drastic changes.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate the reactions to -8 and consider whether to stabilize around this value, given its cautious and collaborative nature, or if necessary, explore slight adjustments downwards to better understand the boundary conditions and ensure all parties' utilities are considered.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to explore the boundary conditions and understand the group's reaction to a larger magnitude while staying within the allowed range.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to adjust based on the feedback, potentially exploring positive magnitudes or stabilizing around a value that seems acceptable to all parties, keeping in mind the goal of maximizing my utility without revealing my exact coefficients.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to move the shared variable slightly higher while staying within the feasible range, considering the group's reaction to previous proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to continue incremental increases or stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to all parties, potentially exploring positive magnitudes to understand the group's preferences and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to make a slight adjustment upwards, maintaining a cautious approach while exploring potential higher utilities for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to stabilize around this value or explore slight adjustments downwards, ensuring that all parties' utilities are considered and maximizing my own utility without revealing my exact coefficients.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis adjustment continues the gradual exploration of higher values, aiming to find a balance that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate reactions to -6 and consider whether to continue incremental increases towards positive values or stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to all parties, keeping in mind the need to balance stability with the potential for higher utilities.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the gradual exploration of higher values, aiming to find a balance that works for all parties. We could move slightly higher from -6, as the group's reactions suggest a comfort with incremental increases.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to introduce a cautious step back, assessing the group's willingness to stabilize at a slightly lower value, which could balance the gradual increase trend with a more prudent approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate reactions to this proposal and consider whether to stabilize around this value, make further slight adjustments downwards if the group seems receptive, or Incrementeally move upwards if the feedback suggests that a higher value is necessary for a consensus, keeping in mind the balance between caution and potential utility gains.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the gradual exploration of higher values while being mindful of the group's comfort with incremental increases.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to stabilize around this value, make further slight adjustments upwards, or explorer larger positive or negative magnitudes to understand the group's preferences and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9-8479-1daffaa4e8bf"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to introduce a cautious step back, assessing the group's willingness to stabilize at a slightly lower value.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate reactions to this proposal and consider whether to stabilize around this value or make further slight adjustments downwards, keeping in mind the balance between caution and potential utility gains.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7a013801-ff2e-4fd9