"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose a cautious move to -1, aiming to find a balance between the group's preferences while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the group's reaction to -1. If there's a strong pushback or a trend towards higher values continues, I might need to adjust my proposal to -2 or lower to protect my utility. If the group seems receptive to -1, I will consider proposing a decrease to -2 or lower in a subsequent turn to further gauge the group's balance point.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a balanced design, aiming to find a stable point that works for everyone, considering the group's convergence around low negative to neutral values. This step seems incremental and reasonable, given the history of proposals and the need for a robust agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "dfd87f0b-2b80-402e-a3c6-318ace76ce37"}, {"answer": "\nLet's confirm our shared range is -10 <= x <= 10. To initiate discussions, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our seed value, allowing us to iteratively refine and find a balanced solution that works for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "71b071e0-5cf8